uying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Johnson Controls International plc, together with its subsidiaries, engages in engineering, manufacturing, commissioning, and retrofitting building products and systems in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia-Pacific. The company designs, manufactures, sells, installs, and services heating, ventilating, air conditioning, controls, building management, refrigeration, integrated electronic security, integrated fire detection and suppression systems, and digital solutions. It also provides energy solutions and technical services, including inspection, scheduled maintenance, and repair and replacement of mechanical and control systems, as well as data-driven building solutions. It serves airport, commercial real estate, data centers, federal government, healthcare, higher education, hospitality, industrial and manufacturing, K-12 education, local government, marine and navy, pharmaceutical, public and affordable housing, sports and entertainment, and state government industries. Johnson Controls International plc was incorporated in 1885 and is based in Cork, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joakim  Weidemanis | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 84K people. Revenue per employee of $306K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $41K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Johnson Controls International  is a large-cap industrials business with a $78.1B market cap on $25.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 33%.","The business throws off $3.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 165% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.6467688531905524},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $18.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-18115296.49},{"text":"Significant goodwill (41% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"27,196 Shares in Johnson Controls International plc $JCI Purchased by Edgestream Partners L.P.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/27196-shares-in-johnson-controls-international-plc-jci-purchased-by-edgestream-partners-l-p.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795170052.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Johnson Controls International plc $JCI Stake Boosted by Focus Advisor Solutions LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/johnson-controls-international-plc-jci-stake-boosted-by-focus-advisor-solutions-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795167903.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.936,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in JCI Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_JCI_Response_111826054002_1795041602.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795041602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Implied Volatility Surging for Johnson Controls International Stock Options","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3031698/implied-volatility-surging-for-johnson-controls-international-stock-options?cid=CS-ZC-FT-tale_of_the_tape%7Coptions-3031698","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795009080.0,"origi